  "full_text": "So you're not supposed to kill the innocent. Earlier, we were talking about ways of, what do you call it, testing people with, we've been talking about this, killing the vile people for a while. And we were thinking of a test, you know, like what would qualify you. Maybe if you, if a person has, let's just say, like, too many cars or something or, you know, I don't know, but there would be just, I was saying the military, I was just saying military officers would be the judge, would write the policy and the military itself would be bitter against, the Lord hears the cry of the poor. The military would be bitter against multiple cars. Anyway, so now I'm not, when I'm adding them to my fold, I'm doing it just by appearance. And you might say, how can that be valid? Well, in the Adam and Eve story, they fled the garden naked, or they realized they were naked, so that your sins are naked. So, you know, it's a kind of interesting thing. Your appearance will change depending on... your state of salvation or something. So you can judge a book by its cover, but that assumes that you're God. Jesus opened the eyes of the blind. So anyway, if you wanted to know how I could justify judging based on looks.",
